; HEX-BoomRider preset - Volatility Boom 400, $20 of headroom on a 10k demo
; Blow line: equity <= 9980 -> alert + halt (reset the demo, or deposit $20 more)
; The numbers below are the whole strategy. One 0.10-lot loss at the 0.30% stop
; costs ~$4.54 = 22.7% of the headroom, so FOUR losses fit in $20 and the 50%
; cap ($10) still admits the broker's minimum lot after the index rises ~2.2x.
; The 0.25% target against that stop pays $3.78 a win and breaks even at a 54.5%
; win rate - the first preset's 0.15/0.40 paid $2.27 for a $6.05 loss and needed
; 72.7%. Sizing takes the minimum lot while the headroom is small, then scales:
; 0.20 lots at ~$45 of headroom, 0.30 at ~$68 (20% of the headroom, floored to
; the 0.10 broker step).
InpBaselineEquity=9980.0
InpRiskPct=20.0
InpMaxRiskPct=50.0
InpTakeProfitPct=0.25
InpStopLossPct=0.30
; --- management: bank the measured target, then let the spike pay more ------
; A stop placed BETWEEN the entry and the target is not a stop, it is a
; take-profit: the target is only ever reached by a SPIKE (a single-tick jump),
; while any intermediate level is reached by ordinary drift - and the drift
; between spikes pulls DOWN, so it gets there first.
; LIVE, 2026-11-02, the previous build proved it: the +0.05% break-even floor sat
; AT the price the moment it armed, so every winner exited at +0.05%, no winner
; ever reached the 0.25% target, not one add fired, and 75 minutes read 4 wins /
; 4 losses, -$14.59 (a 0.05% win against a 0.30% loss is break-even BEFORE the
; spread). Two rules fixed it: the floor may only arm after the target has been
; banked, and no stop may sit closer than InpMinStopGapPct to the price.
; Re-measured on the live-calibrated model (100k ticks x 4 seeds, $20 headroom,
; 0.10 lots; the model's per-tick sigma now comes from that live tape):
;   base engine, banks 0.25%, no adds    $15.93/h   WR .776  PF 2.79  0/4 blown
;   median win +0.250% (the target)      avg win $4.38   avg loss $5.46
;   PRE-FIX floor at +0.05%              median win +0.050% - the live clip
; The ladder itself does nothing at $20: an add at the 0.10 minimum lot needs
; ~$4.50 of this episode's profit in hand, which arrives when the base lot
; reaches 0.30 - i.e. at roughly $68 of headroom. It logs "add-small" until then.
; The 30% ladder cap is what keeps one bad episode inside the 3-loss budget.
InpLockInPct=0.05
InpMinStopGapPct=0.15
InpBackstopTPPct=1.00
InpTrailPct=0.30
InpTrailStartPct=0.40
InpMaxAdds=3
InpAddAtPct=0.20
InpAddRiskPct=100.0
InpMaxLadderLots=0.40
InpMaxLadderRiskPct=30.0
InpMaxSpreadPct=0.03
InpMagic=400400
; The status line is written from a terminal TIMER, not from OnTick, so it keeps
; moving when the chart stops being ticked - and the age of the last tick goes
; inside it. A stale line therefore means the EA is gone; a moving line with a
; climbing tick age means the feed is dead (the container sends ONE alert and
; restarts the terminal after HEX_TICK_STALL_MIN). Nothing here notifies by
; itself: no buzz, no per-minute message.
InpHeartbeatSec=60
InpTickStallSec=300
InpSkipLogSec=60
InpLogDir=HEX-Logs
; Pushes are sent by the CONTAINER (curl -> MT5_NOTIFY_URL), not by the EA:
; MQL5's WebRequest only accepts URLs whitelisted by hand in the terminal GUI,
; which a headless box must not depend on. Leave these two alone.
InpNotifyUrl=
InpNotifyTest=false
